                "reply_count": 11,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Last week, we called on the Biden Administration to end the COVID shot mandate on CMS healthcare workers when the public health emergency expires on May 11. And on Monday of this week, the Biden Administration announced that the COVID shot mandate for CMS-certified healthcare facilities, Federal employees, Federal contractors, and international air travelers will end on May 11! \n\nThis is a win for the American people, a win for medical freedom, and the culmination of years of pushing the Biden Administration to end these draconian mandates.\n\nThe House passed my bill, the Freedom for Health Care Workers Act this year, and I have repeatedly fought the COVID shot mandate at every turn. The authoritarian COVID shot mandates were unscientific and un-American, and I\u2019m glad to see the White House has finally \u201cfollowed the science\u201d to end federal COVID shot mandates on Americans.",
